  "exportLabel": "Molen original Generalife master",
  "expectedDraftMasterHash": "sha256:9eef920398168c32fcf883be8a2a5c23626cd8579e6ec4e654c412229d37bea0",
  "visualBrief": "The Generalife is an open hillside ensemble of tile-roofed pavilions, the long Acequia Court and the Cypress Court double arcade. The Water Stairway climbs toward the Mirador Romántico. Formal planted beds, shallow canals and the open-air theatre extend along the lower garden axis.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 793 m sea-level datum follows the standard viewer terrain. Four small, filled terraces protect flat courts and auditorium geometry from coarse slopes. The remaining landscape follows native elevation.",
  "nativeAxes": "The signed precinct axis points south-southeast along the Generalife gardens. The palace uses a secondary -0.382 rad alignment so the Acequia follows the two mapped channel sections and the cypress court sits on the uphill side.",
  "limitations": [
    "The footprint, channel locations and Water Stairway follow standard PMTiles. Flat court elevations, individual arches, seating and retaining walls are photo-based reconstructions fitted to standard viewer terrain.",
    "Water channels, fountain arcs and garden planting use static geometry and shared materials. Seasonal planting, temporary stage equipment and private interiors are outside the modeled exterior."
  ],
